.TH CREATE-CLASTER-BACKUP.SH 1 "2026-09-24" "pg_claster_creator 2.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
create-claster-backup.sh \- create and rotate non-interactive hot database backups
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B create-claster-backup.sh
.RI [ options ]
.I version cluster database
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B create-claster-backup.sh
calls
.BR create-claster.sh (1)
in non-interactive hot-backup mode for one existing PostgreSQL database.
The default backup directory is read from
.IR .new-claster.config .
.PP
Optional rotation runs only after a successful backup. Files are selected without
opening archives, using the strict mask
.IR VERSION-DATABASE-YYYYMMDD-hhmmss-dmp.tar.gz .
At least the newest matching archive is retained.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " FILE"
Select a trusted configuration file, overriding PGCC_CFG; --config=FILE is also accepted.
Relative paths use the invocation directory. Empty PGCC_CFG means unset.
Missing, unreadable or non-file explicit configs fail without fallback.
Without an explicit choice, prefer the existing per-system config, then the script-local file.
The main script saves only to the selected config; the wrapper retains the choice in sudo/cron.
The builder embeds the selected config and retains its path in last.sh, not in postinst.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print complete usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR -v , " --version"
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BI "--backup-dir " DIRECTORY
Select the backup directory. The configured value or
.I /.postgres/backup
is used by default.
.TP
.BI "--files-cnt " COUNT
Keep at most COUNT archives matching this version and database.
.TP
.BI "--files-size " SIZE
Limit total size of matching archives. SIZE is a positive integer in bytes or
uses B, K/KB/KiB, M/MB/MiB, G/GB/GiB, or T/TB/TiB.
.TP
.B --cron
Interactively create or replace a task below
.IR /etc/cron.d .
The operator must select hourly, daily, weekly, monthly, or a safe custom
five-field numeric cron expression. If no retention option is supplied, the
dialog also requires a file-count or total-size limit.
.SH RETENTION
.B --files-cnt
and
.B --files-size
are mutually exclusive. Rotation never reads backup metadata. Because the hot
archive filename does not contain the cluster name, databases with the same name
and PostgreSQL version share a rotation group when stored in the same directory.
Use separate
.B --backup-dir
values to isolate those tasks.
.PP
When the newest archive alone exceeds a size limit it is preserved and a warning
is printed. A per-version, cluster, and database
.BR flock (1)
prevents concurrent executions of the same task.
.SH CRON FILES
A task is written atomically as
.IR /etc/cron.d/pg-claster-backup-* ,
runs as root, and calls this program without
.BR --cron .
Output is appended to the matching
.IR /var/log/pg-claster-backup-*.log .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
PGCC_CFG selects the configuration file; --config overrides it.
CLI overrides nonempty ENV, then configuration/defaults. Empty ENV is unset.
VERSION CLUSTER DATABASE: PGCC_PG_VERSION, PGCC_CLUSTER_NAME, PGCC_DATABASE;
all three are required without positional arguments. A complete CLI target replaces the ENV target.
--backup-dir: PGCC_BACKUP_DIR; --files-cnt: PGCC_FILES_CNT;
--files-size: PGCC_FILES_SIZE; --cron: PGCC_CRON (yes/no, true/false, 1/0, y/n).
PGCC_CRON=yes still requires interactive scheduling and confirmation.
Count and size limits remain mutually exclusive. Help/version have no ENV aliases.
SQL files and --sql-file are not supported.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/shared/pg_claster_creator/.new-claster.config
Provides the default backup directory. If absent, use .new-claster.config
beside the resolved script, not in the current working directory.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/create-claster-backup.sh
Installed command symlink.
.TP
.I /run/lock/pg-claster-backup-*.lock
Per-task non-blocking lock.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo create-claster-backup.sh 16 subsys asvd
sudo create-claster-backup.sh 16 subsys asvd \
  --backup-dir /BACKUP/postgresql --files-cnt 14
sudo create-claster-backup.sh 16 subsys asvd --files-size 20GiB
sudo create-claster-backup.sh 16 subsys asvd --cron --files-cnt 30
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR create-claster.sh (1),
.BR cron (8),
.BR crontab (5),
.BR flock (1)
